                <h2>Applicable Scenarios and Prerequisites</h2>
<p>This SOP is designed for overseas teams managing Meta (Facebook), Google, TikTok, and other international advertising platforms simultaneously. If you've encountered any of the following issues, this SOP will help you systematically address them:</p>
<ul>
<li>Ads suddenly pausing due to insufficient account balance</li>
<li>Unable to accurately track spending per account after multi-account top-ups</li>
<li>Month-end reconciliation reveals billing discrepancies with no traceable cause</li>
<li>Exchange rate fluctuations causing budget overruns on top-ups</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Prerequisites</strong>: Confirm access to each platform's billing management backend and establish a basic financial ledger template.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Establish Account Fund Health Diagnosis Checklist</h2>
<p>At the beginning of each month, operators must complete an account fund health diagnosis. Diagnostic dimensions include:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Diagnostic Item</th>
<th>Healthy Standard</th>
<th>Warning Threshold</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Days of Balance Coverage</td>
<td>≥ 7 days</td>
<td>&lt; 3 days</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Daily Average Spend (Last 7 Days)</td>
<td>Fluctuation &lt; 20%</td>
<td>Fluctuation &gt; 50%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Billing Cycle Alignment</td>
<td>Top-up timing aligned with billing cycle</td>
<td>Frequent end-of-cycle top-ups</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Card/Wallet Balance</td>
<td>Balance &gt; 50% of monthly average spend</td>
<td>Balance &lt; 20% of monthly average spend</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Operation Steps</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Export 30-day spending reports from each platform</li>
<li>Calculate daily average spend and fluctuation rate</li>
<li>Divide current balance by daily average spend to determine days of coverage</li>
<li>Compare against warning thresholds and flag accounts requiring priority action</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Develop Top-Up Rhythm Planning</h2>
<p>The core principle of top-up rhythm is "advance planning + batched execution," avoiding last-minute large single top-ups.</p>
<p><strong>Standard Top-Up Rhythm</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Weekly Top-Up</strong>: Check balance on a fixed day each week, replenishing to cover 10-14 days of estimated spend</li>
<li><strong>Monthly Forecast</strong>: Complete next month's spend forecast before the 25th of each month, distributing top-up batches according to spending rhythm</li>
<li><strong>Billing Cycle Alignment</strong>: Prioritize billing cycle payments if available (e.g., Net 15/30) to reduce capital occupation</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Case Reference</strong>: A utility app team operating 3 regional accounts set every Tuesday as "Top-Up Day," replenishing to cover 10-14 days of estimated spend each time. After three months, ad pause incidents due to insufficient balance dropped from an average of 6 times per month to 0.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Configure Balance Alert Mechanisms</h2>
<p>Alert mechanisms require coverage at both "manual" and "automated" levels.</p>
<p><strong>Manual Alert Setup</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Set calendar reminders for each account's alert triggers</li>
<li>Flag as "Yellow Alert" when balance falls below 5 days of consumption</li>
<li>Flag as "Red Alert" when balance falls below 3 days of consumption, immediately initiating top-up process</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>System Alert Configuration (Example: Meta Business)</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Navigate to Business Settings &gt; Payments</li>
<li>Enable "Low balance alert" notifications</li>
<li>Set threshold: Recommend setting at 30% of account's weekly average spend</li>
<li>Bind enterprise notification channels (WeChat Work/DingTalk/Email)</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Standardize Financial Reconciliation Workflow</h2>
<p>Financial reconciliation is the final step in fund management and where errors most commonly occur. A "daily + monthly" dual-track system is recommended.</p>
<p><strong>Daily Reconciliation Process</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Export previous day's spending report at 18:00 daily</li>
<li>Cross-compare with top-up records and credit card statements</li>
<li>When discrepancies exceed 2%, record and trace the cause</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Monthly Reconciliation Process</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Export complete billing cycle report at month-end</li>
<li>Verify payable amount against Invoice</li>
<li>If using agents or service providers, confirm rebates/discounts are correctly applied</li>
<li>Archive all reconciliation documents, retaining for at least 12 months</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Common Discrepancy Sources and Handling</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Time Zone Differences</strong>: Platform statistics use different time zones; convert uniformly to UTC or Beijing time</li>
<li><strong>Refund Deductions</strong>: Refunds typically appear in next month's bill; watch for cross-period adjustments</li>
<li><strong>Exchange Rate Fluctuations</strong>: For large top-ups, prioritize rate locks and use in-platform rates for calculations</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 5: Anomaly Risk Identification and Response</h2>
<p>Anomaly risks in fund management primarily fall into three categories:</p>
<p><strong>1. Top-Up Not Received</strong></p>
<p>Response Process:</p>
<ol>
<li>Verify transfer records from bank/payment platform</li>
<li>Confirm recipient account information is correct (Account ID, Payee name)</li>
<li>If not received within 24 hours, immediately contact platform support or agent</li>
<li>Preserve transfer receipts as evidence for appeals</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>2. Abnormal Spend Surge</strong></p>
<p>Response Process:</p>
<ol>
<li>Immediately pause relevant ad groups or campaigns</li>
<li>Investigate whether caused by creative policy changes, delivery configuration errors, or malicious clicks</li>
<li>Complete initial investigation within 30 minutes, sync findings to finance and operations leads</li>
<li>If confirmed as abnormal consumption, collect evidence and submit platform appeal</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>3. Account Restricted or Disabled</strong></p>
<p>Response Process:</p>
<ol>
<li>Immediately screenshot and preserve account status and balance information</li>
<li>Confirm whether account balance can be withdrawn</li>
<li>Submit appeal through official channels while notifying finance to freeze subsequent top-up plans for that account</li>
<li>Adjust delivery strategies for other linked accounts to avoid budget concentration risk</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Operations Metrics Quick Reference Checklist</h2>
<p>The following metrics are recommended for consolidation into weekly operations reports:</p>
<ul>
<li>Account balance and days of coverage for each account</li>
<li>Weekly actual vs. estimated spend deviation rate</li>
<li>Top-up timeliness rate (whether top-ups completed before alert triggers)</li>
<li>Reconciliation discrepancy rate (discrepancy amount / total spend)</li>
<li>Anomaly event response time (hours from discovery to resolution)</li>
</ul>
<p>Consistently tracking these metrics weekly will significantly improve your fund management efficiency and ensure delivery stability.</p>
